    "answer": "The documentation indicates that homing a PSM (Patient-Side Manipulator) involves several considerations:\n\n1. **Homing Zero Position**: The `homing_zero_position` parameter in the configuration schema determines whether the arm should go to a zero position in joint space during the homing procedure. This is typically set to `false` for PSMs by default.\n\n2. **Bug Fixes and Improvements**:\n   - In version 1.1.1, the tolerance for pots to encoder during homing was increased for PSMs.\n   - In version 1.3.0, the engage procedure for sterile adapters and tools was improved, and PID gains were increased for PSMs during homing.\n\n3. **Homing Procedure**: To home the dVRK, you can use the GUI or the ROS topic `home`. During homing, position control starts for all active arms, and MTMs perform a calibration routine.\n\nThese details are sourced from the dVRK documentation and changelogs."
